.TH MU2EDAQ-COMMANDLINE-TOOLS-BOOTSTRAP 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- set up the mu2edaq-commandline-tools venv and CMake build
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates
.I venv/
if it does not exist, upgrades pip/setuptools/wheel, and installs
mu2edaq-commandline-tools into it as an editable install so the checkout is
what runs. Safe to re-run: it is also the "update my dependencies" command.
.PP
With
.B \-\-cpp
it additionally configures and builds the CMake targets
.RB ( mu2edaq_cli_core
and
.BR mu2edaq-tools-info )
under
.IR build/ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Also install the
.I dev
extras (pytest), needed to run the test suite.
.TP
.B \-\-cpp
Configure and build the C++ library and tools with CMake.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Remove
.I venv/
and
.I build/
first.
.TP
.BR \-\-python " \fIPATH\fR"
Interpreter to build the venv with. Default:
.BR $PYTHON ", " python3 .
Python 3.9 or newer is required.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Default interpreter, overridden by
.BR \-\-python .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No usable Python (or, with \-\-cpp, no CMake).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Development setup with tests and the C++ build:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./bootstrap.sh \-\-dev \-\-cpp
source venv/bin/activate
pytest
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-start (1),
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-stop (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
